    {
      "id": "decided",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1260,
      "y": 292,
      "w": 604,
      "h": 372,
      "text": "• Main table on top; dungeon tables below it, like a basement.\n• 3 caves. Break the mobs in front of one to open it; a rail drops the ball into its dungeon.\n• The cave picks the type: each leads to one of the current tier’s 3 types.\n• Each dungeon: own flippers, exit sealed until the encounter is beaten.\n• Every exit pipes back up through the boss cave’s top; wires run down both sides to the inlanes.\n• The lair: a trick shot opens the boss cave only; its layout is random.\n• The main table has 2–3 hand-made layouts; each run picks one.",
      "size": 18,
      "color": "#1f1b16"
    },
